torOS: no full mode set when the desktop takes the laptop's screen over.

wlroots sets the connector's "max bpc" to 8 with its first mode set. The
driver's default is 12, and any change of that property forces a full mode
set (i915 clears mode_changed for a fast set, but not connectors_changed):
the panel is powered off and on again, 1.1 s on the laptop. Measured there:
the mode set takes 19 ms when the value is already 8 and 1.1 s when it is 12.
The panel has 6 bits per colour, so nothing else changes.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c	2026-10-06 07:42:12.481654069 +0300
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dp.c	2026-10-06 07:42:12.482481982 +0300
@@ -6542,6 +6542,18 @@
 	else if (DISPLAY_VER(display) >= 5)
 		drm_connector_attach_max_bpc_property(&connector->base, 6, 12);
 
+	/*
+	 * torOS: start the built-in panel with the "max bpc" the desktop
+	 * asks for (wlroots: 8 for its 8-bit buffers) instead of the largest
+	 * value. A change of this property always costs a full mode set, so
+	 * with the default of 12 the screen went dark for a second when the
+	 * desktop took over from the boot logo.
+	 */
+	if (intel_dp_is_edp(intel_dp) && connector->base.state->max_requested_bpc > 8) {
+		connector->base.state->max_requested_bpc = 8;
+		connector->base.state->max_bpc = 8;
+	}
+
 	/* Register HDMI colorspace for case of lspcon */
 	if (intel_bios_encoder_is_lspcon(dp_to_dig_port(intel_dp)->base.devdata)) {
 		drm_connector_attach_content_type_property(&connector->base);
